This covers the original work: the model logic, calibration, cost assumptions,
code and presentation. The underlying public datasets it draws on (Eskom, NTCSA,
NERSA, DMRE, PyPSA-RSA, Open-Meteo, NASA MERRA-2, OpenStreetMap, Esri) remain
under their own licences and are credited in the application footer.

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode

For commercial licensing enquiries about the original work described above, contact
the author via the repository. Such a licence covers only that work: it cannot cover
third-party data, including NTCSA's GCCA data (see below), which stays under its own
terms.

---

Data sources incorporated in this repository carry their own licences:

- Eskom hourly data (ESK19679 and ESK19243, obtained from the Eskom Data Portal on request; and Eskom's 2021 CSP profile,
  via PyPSA-RSA): no licence of their own, so Eskom's website terms and the Data Portal disclaimer apply: personal,
  educational or non-commercial use only; no reproduction, distribution or publication without Eskom's written consent,
  which has been requested. The raw files are not in this repository; profiles.json and nodal/coal_availability_trace.json
  hold series derived from them, to be replaced with open versions.
- UCT ESRG Single Node Hourly Demand Model (Bruno Merven, ZivaHub):
  https://doi.org/10.25375/uct.24137877 — CC BY 4.0
- PyPSA-RSA network topology and fleet data (Meridian Economics): https://github.com/MeridianEconomics/pypsa-rsa;
  AGPL-3.0-or-later. Its own data-licence table puts its supply-region boundaries under the GCCA's terms (BY-NC-SA). The
  terms for our use are being confirmed with Meridian. The PyPSA library used in validation/ is MIT.
- PVGIS SARAH2 solar profiles: European Commission JRC — open access
- Renewables.ninja wind profiles: Pfenninger & Staffell — CC BY-NC 4.0
- REIPPPP project data (IPP Office, DMRE): no open licence. The IPP Office website terms (May 2016) reserve copyright in
  the site's contents (clause 7.1) and prohibit their unauthorised use (clause 7.2). Used here: project facts (name,
  capacity, technology, location, dates) and figures cited from IPP Office reports, credited.
- GCCA 2025 connection capacity data and supply-area boundaries (NTCSA): NTCSA website terms (June 2024, clauses 2.1, 2.2 and 3.1): non-commercial use only; publication needs NTCSA's written consent.

